# MCNet Rail Wiring Reference v0.9.2

## Standard platform road

```text
approach rail -> D1 detector -> platform -> D2 detector -> H1 locking track -> D3 detector -> next block
```

Inputs: D1 approach, D2 berth/stop, D3 exit.
Output: H1 locking track release.

Fail-safe: H1 unpowered = train held. H1 powered = train released.

## Suggested bundled cable colours

Inputs: white D1, orange D2, magenta D3, light blue spare, yellow occupied, lime emergency, pink manual, gray maintenance.

Outputs: white H1 release, orange signal clear, magenta warning lamp, light blue announcement trigger, yellow maintenance lamp, lime departure bell.

## Intermediate block

```text
detector -> two normal rails -> locking track
```

Most of the time the locking track is already released. It only holds when the next block is occupied, reserved, or unknown.

## Junction controller

Think in routes, not loose switches:

```text
E-CW-OUT
E-ACW-OUT
E-IN-CW
E-IN-ACW
CIRCLE-CW-THROUGH
CIRCLE-ACW-THROUGH
```

A route is allowed only if none of its required track sections or points conflict with another locked route.
